.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt ietf2bibtex 1
.Os ietf2bibtex
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm ietf2bibtex
.Nd Create BibTeX entry for IETF document
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ietf2bibtex
.Op Fl a Ar file | Fl \-authors\-fix\-file Ar file
.br
.Op Fl n | Fl \-no\-authors\-fix\-file
.br
.Op Fl q | Fl \-quiet
.Op Fl w | Fl \-verbose
.br
.Ar document Op Ar ...
.Nm ietf2bibtex
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm ietf2bibtex
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm ietf2bibtex
creates a BibTeX entry for an IETF document (i.e. RFC or Internet Draft). The
necessary information is automatically obtained from online XML references and
the actual document. Note that author names are sometimes wrong, misspelled,
incomplete or inconsistent. Therefore,
.Nm ietf2bibtex
may read a file denoted as
authors fix file. It contains name translations in the form of
"Old Name" "New Name", for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
"A. Bundy"  "Al Bundy"
"J. Muller" "Joe Müller"
"J. Moller" "Jarle Møller"
.Ed
.Pp
Known limitations of
.Nm ietf2bibtex :
.Bl -bullet
.It
IETF metadata and documents only contain ASCII characters. To obtain the
correct non\-ASCII author names (e.g. German, Norwegian, French, etc.), it
is necessary to use authors\-fix.list.
.It
IETF metadata often has wrong or limited author information for a document.
ietf2bibtex tries to obtain the author information from the document.
Unusual formatting sometimes prevents this.
.It
IETF metadata often has the wrong date for a document.
ietf2bibtex tries to obtain the date from the document.
Unusual formatting sometimes prevents this.
.El
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments may be provided:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar document Op Ar ...
The name of the IETF document, e.g. like RFC5351 or draft\-dreibholz\-ipv4\-flowlabel. Multiple names may be provided.
.It Fl a Ar file | Fl \-authors\-fix\-file Ar file
Use the given file as authors fix file.
If not provided, the default is used: try authors\-fix.list in the current
directory first, then /usr/share/doc/bibtexconv/examples/authors\-fix.list.
.It Fl n | Fl \-no\-authors\-fix\-file
Use no authors fix file.
.It Fl q | Fl \-quiet
Print less progress information.
.It Fl w | Fl \-verbose
Print progress information (default).
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints command help.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints program version.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It ietf2bibtex RFC5351
Fetch metadata and create a BibTeX entry for RFC 5351.
.It ietf2bibtex RFC5351 RFC5352 RFC5353 RFC5354 RFC5355 RFC5356 RFC5525 > RSerPool.bib
Fetch metadata for multiple RFC documents and redirect the output to a BibTeX database file.
.It ietf2bibtex \-\-quiet draft\-dreibholz\-ipv4\-flowlabel
Process an Internet Draft quietly without progress output.
.It ietf2bibtex \-\-verbose \-\-authors\-fix\-file /usr/share/doc/bibtexconv/examples/authors\-fix.list draft\-dreibholz\-rserpool\-delay
Process an Internet Draft with explicit author name fixes enabled.
.El
